  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Which of the following regions is *not* connected?",
  "worked_solution": "A region $D$ is connected if every pair of points in $D$ can be joined by a smooth curve or a path in $D.$ \n\nAmong the given options, the only one that does not satisfy this definition is the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14163649/assets/1067a6abc2249b31f3786a3f277a2db10d8f32cbacf971a550a0473243684da7.png)\n\n \n\nNote that if we take two points $P$ and $Q$, as shown below, there is no path lying entirely within the region that connects them.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14163649/assets/2bcaaf15d709d6396155bcdc9e8976bb037c9f341fc0b8863687958dbb0f40ff.png)",
